# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated artifacts. sim/build/ also covers the per-job subdirectories
# tools/run.mjs makes -- sim/build/interp, sim/build/basic and so on --
# so thirteen suites can compile basic.bin at once without racing.
sim/build/
build/

# The Rust fast runner's build output. Cargo.lock is committed;
# rust/src/optab.rs is generated but committed, gated by mkrsopc --check.
rust/target/

# Node is the task runner only (package.json + tools/run.mjs); there are
# no dependencies, so there is nothing here to commit. package-lock.json
# is deliberately *not* ignored: if a dependency ever appears, its lock
# belongs in the tree.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
badapple.mp4
demos/bapple/

# Web build outputs (built fresh by tools/mkweb.py in CI)
web/*.wasm
web/*.bin
web/*.img
web/*.json

# Upstream sources, cloned rather than vendored. `tools/ucsd-psystem-os`
# and `tools/ucsd-psystem-vm` are Peter Miller's reconstruction of the
# UCSD p-System and its VM, and they carry their own .git -- committing
# them would nest a repository inside this one and add 5.4 MB of
# somebody else's history. sim/test_pascal.py reads system.vol out of
# the VM tree; clone it there before running that suite.
/tools/ucsd-psystem-os/
/tools/ucsd-psystem-vm/

# The Z-Machine story files and the reference ZIL sources. Infocom's
# games are commercial software and are not ours to redistribute, and
# z3/ref/ is three more cloned repositories. sw/z3/ is the interpreter
# and it is committed; the stories are not, and tools/gen_z3.py names
# the ones it wants.
/z3/

# The demo disc the suites build at the repo root. sim/test_pascal.py
# and sim/test_z3.py write it, `python tools/mkdemos.py` makes it, and
# it is 8 MB of flash image with the Infocom stories inside it.
/demos.img

# `pip install -e .` leaves this behind.
*.egg-info/

# Miss Coolman: ripped reference art, private -- never committed
assets/misscool/
